  "138": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Video 1> is the source video for the edit: one continuous handheld shot of a man dancing on a flat grey rooftop under an overcast sky, with brick factory buildings, a tall brick chimney and a city skyline behind him.\n<Subject 1> is the dancer in <Video 1>: a bearded man in a black tracksuit with red stripes on the sleeves and black sneakers, selected for replacement.\n<Subject 2> is a knight in full polished steel plate armour with a closed visor helmet topped by a red plume and a red cloth tabard over the breastplate, replacing <Subject 1>.\n\nsummary:\n[video editing] The target video is an edited version of <Video 1>. <Subject 2> replaces <Subject 1> and performs exactly the same dance on the same rooftop, while the rooftop, the brick buildings, the chimney, the cloudy sky, the handheld camera and the timing of <Video 1> are kept.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Video 1> (rooftop setting, camera movement and timing): partially_preserved - keep the rooftop, the background buildings, the chimney, the overcast light, the framing, the handheld camera movement and the exact timing of every move; change only the dancer.\n<Subject 1>: removed - the man in the black tracksuit does not appear in any frame of the target video.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): attribute_transfer - the knight takes over every step, arm wave, body pop, squat and pose of the dance of <Subject 1>, in the same positions and at the same moments.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video keeps the live-action, overcast, slightly desaturated look of <Video 1>.\n[Shot 1] Follow the framing, the handheld camera movement and the action timing of <Video 1>. On the grey rooftop, in front of the brick factory buildings and the tall chimney, <Subject 2> dances in place of <Subject 1>: the knight in polished steel plate armour, closed visor and red-plumed helmet sweeps his armoured arms out wide, pops his chest, raises one gauntlet high, drops into a wide squat and steps from side to side exactly as the original dancer does, the red tabard swinging with each move and the cloudy daylight sliding across the steel. Only the knight is visible, from the first frame to the last.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nMetal plates clank and scrape in time with every step and arm movement, steel boots ring on the rooftop, and a steady city wind blows over the roof with distant traffic far below.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nAn upbeat hip-hop drum beat at a moderate tempo with a deep kick and a crisp snare that hits on the sharpest moves."
    },
